\subsection{Impact of Lyapunov Penalty Factor ($\beta$)}
To understand the sensitivity of the Lyapunov penalty factor $\beta$, we evaluated the agent's performance across varying $\beta$ values ($\beta \in \{0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 3.0\}$). As illustrated in Fig. \ref{fig:beta}, setting $\beta$ too high (e.g., $\beta > 3.0$) results in an overly conservative policy that sacrifices visual quality (VMAF) to maintain a full buffer. Conversely, a near-zero $\beta$ negates the safety constraint, increasing the risk of rebuffering to levels similar to pure PPO. Our empirical tuning demonstrates that $\beta = 1.5$ strikes the optimal Pareto balance between maximizing QoE and ensuring playback stability.

