\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
We presented a Future-Aware PPO agent for adaptive video streaming. By incorporating immediate future chunk sizes into the state space and utilizing Lyapunov optimization, our agent learns a robust policy that balances visual quality and playback stability. Experimental results demonstrate that our method achieves MPC-level competitive QoE while substantially mitigating instability, offering a 3x reduction in switching frequency and a 60\% drop in rebuffering compared to aggressive control-theoretic approaches. Furthermore, it strictly outperforms standard pure RL baselines by 2.1\% in overall QoE. This work highlights the importance of "short-term foresight" combined with heuristic penalty-shaping in reinforcement learning for systems control. In future work, we plan to extend this hybrid framework to live video streaming scenarios where future chunk sizes must be dynamically forecasted, and explore the dynamic adaptation of the reference buffer threshold ($B_{ref}$) based on real-time network volatility.

